# counter harness. One force call is one RgpotCounter.calculate entry.
# geomeTRIC finite-difference Hessians are not used.
# v2 success is under the cap, at the force stop, and Hessian index 0.
# energy and Kabsch RMSD were not applied: the problem file has no energy_tol, rmsd_tol, or per-start reference.
# LJ38 index removes the six rigid modes. A curvature is negative only below -max(force_norm, 1e-8*||H||_F, 1e-6).
# final coordinate system: CartesianCoordinates 3, DelocalizedInternalCoordinates 997
# TRIC coordinates, DelocalizedInternalCoordinates with connect false and addcart false. Bonds are the two nearest neighbors. The covalent-radius graph is not used: pairs inside 1 Angstrom would be bonded and the primitive G matrix does not finish on these starts. Atoms are labeled H so Schlegel's guess stays positive near sigma. The stop, trust radius, and Hessian policy match the Cartesian row. A failed coordinate rebuild can continue in Cartesian coordinates, which is the library recovery.
